.AVIATION...
(18Z TAFS)
Issued at 128 PM PDT Mon Oct 26 2026

Satellite imagery shows clear skies for much of the region with some
stratocu clouds lingering around the North Bay. Sites are still
reporting VFR conditions and this should hold through the evening.
There isn`t much change in the pattern today, so expect to see
similar conditions tonight as we did last night. A mix of VFR and
MVFR ceilings are forecast, the question being if we get a round of
IFR or LIFR conditions again. Confidence is high for the mix of VFR
and MVRF cigs, but low to moderate for KSTS staying VFR tonight.

Vicinity of SFO...Winds will remain breezy through the afternoon and
evening hours with gusts peaking around 20-25kt. Winds should
gradually ease after sunset, with the forecast challenge becoming
ceiling heights. Like last night, models flirt MVFR cigs around the
vicinity of SFO. Given there isn`t much of a pattern change, expect
the forecast to be on repeat tonight. If that is the case, we may
see BKN MVFR cigs from 12-16Z VFR conditions returning after that.
Another breezy afternoon and evening is expected for Tuesday with
wind gusts up to 20-25kt possible.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...VFR conditions should prevail for the
afternoon and evening hours and be accompanied with breezy onshore
winds. Gusts look to be peak between 18-22kt around the Bay, before
decreasing late in the evening. Much like the discussions above,
models show MVFR cigs flirting around the Bay. Kept the trend of
them arriving early Tuesday morning clearing out around or just
after sunrise.

